Z||000000||Monkeyman||05-16-2000||11:18 AM||||I just recovered the headliner from the Monkeymobile (I wanted the 3rd brake light).  I cut and glued around the edges (what a pain).  My problem is that I'm not sure exactly where or how to cut out the sunroof section.  I don't want to cut too much, but I see the groove the material needs to get stuffed into, so I don't want to leave too much either.  Any one have thier headliner out and can post a pic of exactly what the extra material should look like?  I knew I should have taken some pics before I pulled the old material off, but I didn't think about it.  (Stupid me! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">)||||reg||5
Z||000001||Carrolles||05-16-2000||01:45 PM||||Leave about an inch and a half all around.  You can trim off the excess after you stuff it into the groove.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||05-16-2000||03:47 PM||||Yep thats it,  what Carrolles said.<P>"Better to have too much than not enough"<P>I did my 87 not to long ago, you can leave as much as you want, and trim after. It's an easy job and looks good, you'll love it and ask why I didn't do it a long time ago!!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by DXR_DAD (edited 05-16-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000003||fierodave||05-17-2000||02:12 AM||||One more point Monk.......  don't cut it out until it's installed,  It will help to hold the board together during install,  You did clean and seal the old board with a polyurathane finish right? :~)<BR>If you didn't. you may be doing it again in the near future<BR>FD||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||05-17-2000||09:24 AM||||Umm...Oops!  I didn't clean it at all (thought about this this am as I noticed the new material starting to come off already <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">) and I didn't know anything about a poly finish.  What's up with that?  I guess I need to carefully remove the material and start all over again.  I just noticed that the headliner is starting to crack.  Damn.  I didn't really want to buy another one for $175 from the Fiero Store.||||reg||1
